A||N||9||Seanh||86GT Subwoofer||||9||
Z||000000||Seanh||07-11-2000||04:01 PM||||I have an 86 Fiero, I have installed an aftermarket streo/cd player. I did not know that my car had an Amp. or 5.25inch subwoofers. I didnt hook up my remote on lead from my stero because I dont have an auto anntana. Well i just found out that this turns on that amp I never knew I had. So I get them all running and am driving the car right after and one of the subs blew. This is understandable after 15 years. Pontiac has discontinued makeing these small subwoofer, and I dont know of any stero company that make subs that small. If I cant get new subs, I would like to replace these with regular speakers. BUT, I dont know of any other place to put a sub(s). I would like to hear any suggestions from people who have installed new subs in there car. Or I would like to get in touch with somone who would like to sell their working factory subs. Thanks||||reg||9
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||07-11-2000||04:32 PM||||Rodney Dickman sells a speaker replacement for the subwoofer.  Here is his site  <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/</A>  .  I don't think its on his site yet, but I talked to him on the phone and he has them for sale.  I'm probably going with one as soon as I figure out what head unit I want.<P>I can vouch for his other products, espically his comp short shifter, A++<P><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||07-11-2000||05:02 PM||||for you both -- I have one of Rodney's sub speaker replacements here and it is a perfect replacement - right size, good sound, he also has the foam pads that fit between the speaker and the sub housing grill -- I don't know if he has them on his site yet or if he has priced them yet either but I would recommend it!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||07-11-2000||05:06 PM||||oh, here are photos of the speaker  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sub_speaker.jpg">  and the sub box repair pads  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sub_repair_pads.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||07-11-2000||05:06 PM||||Thanks so much, I just ordered 2 new subs from him. I am happy to know that they are so highly recommended. I would also still like to hear from some people that have installed bigger subs in their car. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||286SE'S||07-11-2000||05:38 PM||||Why order two? Are you reading the Haynes manual that says there are two of them in the car? Have fun trying to find the other one. They must have been copying the Firebird manual (it has two subs).<BR>When replacing the sub speaker, remove the dash speaker above it. There is a 10" port tube that you can pull off before trying to lower the exclosure out of the dash. I cracked mine pulling the box down. It will fall off anyway and you need access to get it back on. Have fun.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||07-11-2000||05:43 PM||||you can remove the sub enclosure without removing the dash speaker with just a little care -- ease it out and move the bottom of the sub enclosure to the left as you are lowering it -- if the tube cracks, wrap it tightly with electrical tape and I'll guarantee you a snug fit that won't come off when you replace it. Just remember, the tube fits to the left when replacing it......I have taken mine out many times (tried different speakers in it.......liked Rodney's the best too!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||wkayl||07-11-2000||08:34 PM||||Are you sure you blew your subwoofer.  I did the same thing as you and what happened is it shorted out the power antenna circuit in the radio.  It just made a kind of a  buzzing noise throught the woofer.  Here is the site I found to wire it correctly to work. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.radio.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.radio.html</A>   ||||reg||1
Z||000008||BBBAD GT||07-11-2000||10:14 PM||||tgowens:  Did you hear a difference witht he stock amp hooked to the sub, or did you change that out too?  My stock sub isn't worth a darn, and I'm thinking a new speaker like Rodneys and a new little amp should do the trick, anybody agree?  I'm also thinking of the head unit Cliff bought, which should complete the system.  <P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||tgowens||07-11-2000||10:24 PM||||BBBAD GT, I heard a difference even with the stock amp (all I have ever used. Rodney's speaker has a deeper tone and has a lower range than the stock speaker. For what it's worth, Radio Shack sells a 5 1/2" sub-woofer speaker too for about $12 but the tone wasn't anything like Rodney's. I also upgraded to an AM/FM/CD unit with a 7-band equalizer from a '98 Grand AM -- between the equalizer and the sub slider switch, it is quite a bit of bass for a 5 1/2" speaker -- personally, the stock amp is more than enough to drive that little speaker.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
